 > **Note:** The prices used will be accurate at the time of access, but they can still change over time.
 
+## Customer-specific pricing (optional)
+
+By default OpenCost uses the Azure Billing Rate Card API, which returns list prices. To use customer-specific prices from your Azure billing account, OpenCost can additionally download the Azure consumption price sheet. This path is optional and is enabled by setting a billing account.
+
+Set the following environment variables on the OpenCost deployment (or supply the equivalent values via the `CustomPricing` configuration):
+
+| Variable | Description |
+| --- | --- |
+| `AZURE_BILLING_ACCOUNT` | Azure Billing Account ID. When set, OpenCost attempts to download customer-specific prices from the price sheet API in addition to the rate card path. |
+| `AZURE_OFFER_ID` | Azure Offer ID used when querying pricing. |
+
+> **Note:** The price sheet API is not yet officially supported by the Azure Go SDK, so OpenCost implements a client in the style of the SDK. This will be replaced once official support is available.
+
